BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Angels in America\, Part One: Millennium Approaches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T230000
DTSTAMP:20261103T193658Z
UID:funcheap-1641049@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerPhoto by Crystal LiuIn the fir
 st part of Tony Kushner’s Pulitzer-winning epic\, set in 1980’s New Yo
 rk City\, a gay man is abandoned by his lover when he contracts the AIDS v
 irus\, and a closeted Mormon lawyer’s marriage to his pill-popping wife 
 stalls. Other characters include the infamous McCarthy-ite lawyer Roy Cohn
 \, Ethel Rosenberg\, a former drag queen who works as a nurse\, and an ang
 el.\nBetween its 1993 Broadway premiere and its 2017 National Theatre revi
 val\, Angels’ mythical status has expanded\, onstage and off. But to dir
 ector and actor John Fisher\, this play is best experienced when presented
  up close\, with its human heartbreaks and joys mere feet from the audienc
 e. “[Theatre Rhinoceros] is ‘IMAX’ theatre – it’s immediate\, it
 ’s right there\, you could touch the actors. It’s always been staged a
 s an epic\, as opposed to a lived experience. And I don’t believe it was
  written as an epic\, it was written as a ‘fantasia’ – and fantasy i
 s immersive\, not witnessed.”\n\n$40.00\n\nTickets: https://therhino.aud
 ience1st.com/store/8\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/angels-america-part
 -millennium-approaches/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/ANGELS
 -Promo-7.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T193658Z
LOCATION:Theatre Rhinoceros\, 4229 18th St\, San Francisco
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/angels-america-part-millennium-approaches/
END:VEVENT
