CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerThe MarshWritten & Performed b
 y Janet Thornburg\nDirected & Developed by David Ford\nCoached by Tina D
 ’Elia\n7:30pm Fridays\, November 6 – December 11\, 2026\n\nFresh off a
  sold-out\, award-winning first look at The Marsh’s In Front of Your Eye
 s Performance Festival\, Playwright and Performer Janet Thornburg‘s Cogn
 itive Divine will have its world premiere at The Marsh San Francisco Studi
 o this fall. In this rollicking autobiographical comedy\, Janet moves from
  Colorado to San Francisco in 1972\, where a closed-head injury\, late-in-
 life love\, even-later-in-life parenthood\, and a divorce await her\, alon
 g with a right-wing coup led by one of the seven subpersonalities in her p
 syche. Wild Child\, Rosie\, and Mauve love San Francisco\; Raisin and Hann
 ah want to go home. Cora soothes Raisin with cinnamon rolls while Hannah f
 rets about sugar. Hannah and Wild Child clash over partying. Rosie wants n
 ew clothes and skin care\; Mauve wants writers’ conferences. Add the sho
 ck of becoming an elder\, and something has got to give.\nTicket Informati
 on:\nTickets: $25 – $35 General Seating | $50 & $100 Reserved Seating\n6
 0 minutes | No Intermission | Ages 14+ (Please do not bring infants to the
  show)\n\n$25.00\n\nTickets: https://eventvesta.com/events/168648/t/ticket
 s\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/janet-thornburgs-cognitive-divine-2/\n
 Source: Funcheap SF
