 -friendly Día de los Muertos & Diwali event in the park. Celebrated annua
 lly in the fall season\, these two distinct cultural observances come toge
 ther in a national park to honor South Asian and Latinx traditions. Design
 ed intentionally as a celebration and a learning opportunity\, attendees a
 re invited to participate in a wide range of activities that include arts 
 and crafts\, storytelling\, cultural dance\, song\, and a fire ceremony\, 
 and learn about social and environmental justice issues in both cultures.\
