DESCRIPTION:Culture & Diversity Film Festival presents:\n\nSHORT FILMS on 
 “LOVE\, FOOD & FREEDOM”\n\nKosherSoul\n\nCulinary historian and author
  Michael Twitty brings together a diverse team of chefs of color to presen
 t a historic communal meal rooted in African American\, Jewish\, and diasp
 oric culinary traditions in this Silver Telly Award-winning documentary fi
 lm.\n\nMise en Place\n\nVeteran dramatic filmmaker Andrew Kadikian present
 s the story of a chef who has lost his passion but finds new inspiration i
 n an unexpected place.\n\nVariety Club\n\nDesperate to grow up and leave a
  camp for kids with disabilities\, a young woman with Down syndrome plots 
 her escape with a potential suitor.\n\nDeepa\n\nA woman nearing 60 with de
 ep ties to her community in a thriving and active South Asian neighborhood
  comes to terms with emotions of love and loss.\n\nLove Will Set You Free\
 n\nA group of actors workshop and then present a musical stage play explor
 ing the meaning of the “Antebellum\, Interracial\, Intergenerational\, I
 ntersectional\, Fully Sexual\, Unbelievably True Tale of How the Power of 
 Love Will You Free.”\n\nalso\n\nSHORT DOCUMENTARIES on “SPORTS\, DREAM
 S & SAILING”\n\nShuttle\n\nA Thai badminton player takes on the challeng
 es of a sports scholarship in Beijing along with academic and family strug
 gles in passionate pursuit of a dream.\n\nGrassroots Drifter\n\nA teenage 
 driver is born to drift. This sport of drifting is gaining traction in Chi
 na\, with drivers of all ages pursuing the exhilarating compe00on of two c
 ars dramaticall...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/cultu
 re-diversity-film-festival-short-films-on-love-food-freedom-and-sports-dre
 ams-sailing-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
