BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE MUSIC: School Fair\, goldenstar\, Poor Image
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T220000
DTSTAMP:20261104T195100Z
UID:dothebay-17866863@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Throwin’ Bo’s presents:\n\nSchool Fair\n\nSchool Fair (Fin
 dlay Buchanan\, Semisi Ma’ia’i\, Hamish Morgan\, De Stevens and Rose P
 ickernell) make music embedded in the human experience. It’s a product o
 f the band’s native New Zealand\, a place that remains intimate and remo
 te\, where emotion is magnified over both distance and familiarity. The fi
 ve band members began the project renting out a factory-sized\, sub-zero d
 egree Celsius room normally operated by construction workers in the indust
 rial area of Ōtepoti\, Dunedin\, New Zealand in 2021\, recording music on
  the 4-track tape recorder that would become debut Gorse on a Hill. The al
 bum remained the only trace of the band online for a few years\, an artifa
 ct for those who know where to look. School Fair’s music has this sense 
 of self-discovery when you find it\, a sound that feels both recognizable 
 and like the vacant expanse of a country whirring by on a train. Still wit
 h little to no self-promotion\, the appearance of sophomore effort Bird th
 e Kid online in early 2025 was a new portal to their world of melodic and 
 intricate indie music that retains a kind of atmospheric beauty.\n\nUnexpe
 cted Violence (Mutual\, 2026) is the first record made between geographica
 l places\, with the band now split in between London and New Zealand. You 
 can hear this fragmented approach in the patchwork quality and inherent co
 nnective tissue of the album. Recorded initially in a studio in East Londo
 n\, it was the first time the band brought in an outside engineer (S...\n\
 nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.co
 m%2Fe%2F2001417665113%3Faff%3Doddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://dothebay.com
 /events/2026/11/12/live-music-school-fair-goldenstar-poor-image-tickets\nS
 ource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.782364;-122.482951
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34540268/39345c8e-f33b-4c04-80b1-31acfff68a77.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T195100Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/12/live-music-school-fair-goldenst
 ar-poor-image-tickets
END:VEVENT
