DESCRIPTION:"The Banner"\n\nIn an effort to raise awareness of the band\, 
 Matt and Jay drop a huge banner across from The Rivoli. Unfortunately\, it
  turns out to be more revealing than they'd planned.\n\n"The Booking"\n\nM
 att and Jay form a secret undercover plan to sneak in to the local Toronto
  newspaper listings so they can try to book their own gig.\n\n"The Bean"\n
 \nMatt and Jay are left wondering if Christmas miracles exist when they tr
 y to get their own float into the Santa Claus parade and face issues at ev
 ery turn.\n\n"The Blindside"\n\nMatt prepares for the release of the next 
 Star Wars movie by watching the original trilogy. However\, after sitting 
 for too long in front of the TV\, Matt goes blind on the day of the premie
 re.\n\nThis film can be used with loyalty cards or our 2026 annual CinemaS
 FBay passes\n\n"The Big Time"\n\nMatt convinces Jay that to book a gig at 
 the Rivoli\, they need to make a film. Matt sneaks it into Sundance\, beco
 ming a pseudo-celebrity and spiralling out of control.\n\n"The Boy"\n\nMat
 t and Jay befriend a sick kid to use his final wish to ask for Nirvanna th
 e Band to play the Rivoli. They wind up showing him the time of his life\,
  but will time run out?\n\n"The Buffet"\n\nJay writes Matt a letter saying
  that he intends to leave the band\; over a feast at an all-you-can-eat Ch
 inese buffet\, Jay tries to work up the courage to read Matt the letter.\n
 \n"The Bank"\n\nMatt and Jay find themselves unwitting and unwilling parti
 cipants in a hostage situation. Instead of a crisis\, Matt sees an opportu
 ...\n\n$30\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20090?s
 iteToken=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/
 2026/11/13/nirvanna-the-band-the-show-season-one-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
 \n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://dancersgroup.org/calendar/29th-anniversary-
 san-francisco-transgender-film-festival/2026-11-13/1/?utm_source=caldiscov
 ery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca\n- https://dancersgroup.o
 rg/calendar/29th-anniversary-san-francisco-transgender-film-festival/2026-
 11-13/2/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco
 -ca
