BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NEIL YOUNG CELEBRATION: Live Music Tribute & Screening of Rust Nev
 er Sleeps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T213000
DTSTAMP:20261109T222818Z
UID:dothebay-18053745@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Neil Young Celebration\n\nNeil Young Tribute from local musici
 ans plus a screening of Rust Never Sleeps\n\nTo celebrate the 81st birthda
 y of one of our all-time favorites\, a group of local musicians are coming
  together to honor the iconic work of Neil Young. The set will be followed
  by a screening of his iconic San-Francisco-set concert film Rust Never Sl
 eeps.\n\nSinger/songwriter Neil Young is sometimes visionary\, sometimes f
 laky\, sometimes both at once\, but he has never been boring. Indeed\, Nei
 l Young has weathered runs of critical and popular ambivalence only to be 
 vindicated by being periodically "rediscovered" by young musicians and fan
 s. He has maintained a large following since the early '70s with music in 
 three basic styles — solo acoustic ballads\, sweet country rock\, and lu
 mbering garage rock (with some experimental music side trips)\, all topped
  by his high voice — and he veers from one to another in unpredictable p
 hases. His subject matter also shifts from personal confessions to allusiv
 e stories to bouncy throwaways. A dedicated primitivist\, Young is constan
 tly proving that simplicity is not always simple.\n\nRust Never Sleeps is 
 a concert film shot on Neil Young's 1978 U.S. tour\, filmed at the Cow Pal
 ace in San Francisco. Divided into two segments\, acoustic and electric\, 
 the film is Young at his best\, shown just why the grunge generation holds
  him in such high esteem\, and that not all 60's heroes were burnt out by 
 the mid-70's.\n\nDOORS at 7:00 PM | MUSIC at 7:30 PM | MOVIE...\n\nTickets
 : https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20292?siteToken=d2atbcege5kn
 qsavntt91g1250\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/13/neil-young
 -celebration-live-music-tribute-screening-of-rust-never-sleeps-tickets\nSo
 urce: DoTheBay
GEO:37.782364;-122.482951
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35376686/97eb8a98-c453-4fe9-b914-beaaa02e10ac.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T222818Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/13/neil-young-celebration-live-mus
 ic-tribute-screening-of-rust-never-sleeps-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prokofiev’s “Romeo & Juliet” w/ the SF Symphony (Nov. 13–1
 5)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T223000
DTSTAMP:20261110T072652Z
UID:funcheap-1646666@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Prokofiev’s “Romeo & Juliet” w/ the SF Symphony (Nov. 13
 –15)\nSF Symphony\nProkofiev’s ballet music for Romeo and Juliet is ev
 ery bit as singular as the Shakespeare tragedy that inspired it: Savage an
 d sensual\, tragic and comic\, it conveys all the passion of the play and 
 loses none of its ambiguity. Debuting French conductor Marie Jacquot leads
  the Orchestra in the first SF Symphony performances of Andromède\, by he
 r underrated fellow countrywoman Augusta Holmès.\nThe symphonic poem infu
 ses ancient Greek myth with Wagnerian grandeur. Inspired by the music of e
 arly Christianity\, Ottorino Respighi pulls off medieval plainsong with 20
 th-century pizzazz in his spellbinding Concerto gregoriano. Japanese violi
 nist Sayaka Shoji summons up all of its enormous expressive power.\nProkof
 iev’s Romeo and Juliet\nFriday-Sunday\, November 13-15\nDavies Symphony 
 Hall\, 201 Van Ness Ave. SF\nGet Tickets – Tickets start at $30 – Orch
 estra seats start at just $69!\nSchedule:\n\nFriday\, November 13 – 7:30
 pm\nSaturday\, November 14 – 7:30pm\nSunday\, November 15 – 2pm\n\nArt
 ists\n\nMarie Jacquot – Conductor\nSayaka Shoji – Violin\nSan Francisc
 o Symphony\n\nProgram\n\nAugusta Holmès – Andromède – First San Fran
 cisco Symphony Performances\nOttorino Respighi – Concerto gregoriano\nSe
 rgei Prokofiev – Selections from Romeo and Juliet\nProgram Book\n\nConce
 rt Extras\nAn Inside Music Talk with members of the SF Symphony will be pr
 esented on stage one hour before each concert. Free to all ticketholders.\
 nInside Music Video Talk with Jenn...\n\n$30.00\n\nTickets: https://www.sf
 symphony.org/Buy-Tickets/2026-27/Romeo-and-Juliet\nDetails: https://sf.fun
 cheap.com/prokofievs-romeo-juliet-w-the-sf-symphony-nov-13-15/\nSource: Fu
 ncheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/349830
 -26_PMAX_RomeoJuliet_1-1200x628-1-e1794278364269.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T072652Z
LOCATION:Davies Symphony Hall\, 201 Van Ness Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 9410
 2
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/prokofievs-romeo-juliet-w-the-sf-symphony-nov-
 13-15/
END:VEVENT
