BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE MUSIC: Dagmar Zuniga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T220000
DTSTAMP:20261104T195100Z
UID:dothebay-17685841@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Throwin’ Bo’s presents:\n\nDagmar Zuniga\n\nNicaraguan-Ame
 rican artist Dagmar Zuniga makes music that feels both intimate and expans
 ive: songs drift like disrupted signals\, carried by harmony\, tape hiss\,
  and a strong sense of touch. Her debut solo album in filth your mystery i
 s kingdom / far smile peasant in yellow music — written and recorded in 
 New York\, Norway\, and Athens\, Georgia over a period of five years on he
 r longtime companion\, the Tascam 424 — was released by the People’s C
 oalition of Tandy on Bandcamp & YouTube in January 2025\, accompanied by a
  small tape run that sold out instantly. The project quickly garnered over
  two hundred thousand views and the attention of artists such as Mount Eer
 ie\, who invited her to tour with them that summer.\n\nThis year\, what wa
 s once a jewel of tapped-in algorithms and message boards will meet the wo
 rld at large\, with in filth arriving digitally on March 4\, and physicall
 y on April 10\, via AD 93.\n\nin filth is an atmospheric\, devotional coll
 age where one voice multiplies into a chorus of selves\, sometimes delicat
 e\, sometimes severe\; an effect created by Zuniga’s masterful layering 
 of texture and complex harmonies. Synths glitter out like spears of sunlig
 ht from beneath clouds of moody\, time-distorted guitars\, and songs spin 
 about themselves like tightly-wound music boxes\, making use of a kind of 
 hypnotic repetition\, before melting apart into their components or slippi
 ng into the following track.\n\nZuniga began recording to tape as a teenag
 e...\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventb
 rite.com%2Fe%2F1994135678495%3Faff%3Doddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://dothe
 bay.com/events/2026/12/5/live-music-dagmar-zuniga-tickets\nSource: DoTheBa
 y
GEO:37.782364;-122.482951
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33673273/a52f0622-7d8d-4689-9758-e92772f209cc.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T195100Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/5/live-music-dagmar-zuniga-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T140000
DTSTAMP:20261102T193355Z
UID:funcheap-1645561@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:“Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)\n
 Lindy in the Park\nGet ready to swing in Golden Gate Park every sunny Sund
 ay at “Lindy in the Park\,” a weekly free event near the de Young Muse
 um\, when the streets of Golden Gate Park are closed to traffic and the da
 ncers take over.\nThis in person event resumed June 20\, 2021\nLindy in th
 e Park | Free Outdoor Swing Dance & Lessons\nEvery Sunday | 11 am to 2 pm\
 nJFK Dr. btwn 8th and 10th\, behind the De Young Museum\, Golden Gate Park
 \, SF\nFREE\nRain and Bay to Breakers cancels\, but other than that\, Lind
 y in the Park takes place every Sunday – even on holidays – so even if
  New Year’s Day\, Christmas\, or Fourth of July falls on a Sunday\, they
 ’ll be out there dancing. On the very rare occasion when they cancel\, t
 hey’ll make a new posting on their website\, usually by 10am on Sunday. 
 Lindy in the Park’s Schedule FAQ\n\nFree Beginners Swing Lessons | Noon 
 to 12:30 pm\nLindy in the Park offers a free weekly beginning swing dance 
